error[LM-G003]: in `Block`, the repeated `Entry` and what follows it both start with `Entry`, so the parser cannot tell where the repetition ends
  --> broken/broken.langmeld:12:6
   |
12 | rule Block     = "{" Entry* Entry? "}"
   |      ^^^^^
   = note: In technical terms: the choice between going on and stopping is made by looking at most 3 tokens ahead (LL(3)), and both ways can begin with `Entry`.
   = note: To fix this, factor out the common start, for example by ending the repeated part with `;` or with a lookahead such as `&"}"`, or use `try` / `extern rule`.

